{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083601-batini-and-iran","id":1083601,"title":"batini and iran..","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-25T12:04:49-07:00","id":1083601,"title":"batini and iran..","content":"so.. batini are presented as spiritual yet enlightened scholars who believe in unity but also some individuality... yet ruhollah khomenei was explicitly one of them.<br /> now i know the technocracy has a lot of power over media..but somehow i doubt that the wod version of the islamic republic of iran is a more tolerant enlightened place.<br /> <br /> any thoughts/?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T13:16:31-07:00","id":1083635,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, Islam is a bit more complex that usually presented by either apologists or detractors in the Western media, and I make <i>absolutely no</i> claims at being any sort of expert, but the over all impression that I get is that most Mages who follow Islam tend to be followers of Sufism, which is (again, generally speaking) a more internally focused facet of the faith than the Sharia/Fiqh focused fundamentalist political movements (Iran's Velayati-e faqih &quot;rule by jurist&quot; system or the Sunni Salafist movement).<br /> <br /> I have no idea about the concept of Ayatollah Ruballah Khomeini's alleged involvement with the Ahl i Batin. I would presume it's an artifact left over from the days of when numerous historical figures were shoehorned into various WoD factions (I'm looking at you, 1st ed Cult of Ecstasy Tradition book). Or it may be something super goofy from the Lost Paths book. I don't know.<br /> <br /> Modern Iran is effectively a totalitarian theocracy with totalitarian democracy window dressing, meaning that the Shia clergy controls the government and dictates everything, with the regular meaningless show election that doesn't really impact anything. The law does not recognize the existence of homosexuals, only heterosexuals engaging in sodomy (which until 2012 was punishable by death; now it's 100 lashes for being the top, and death for being the bottom unless he repents, then he just gets 100 lashes; lesbians can still be put to death on the 4th offense); Adultery while married is punishable by death; Blasphemy can be punishable by death; &quot;Waging War Against God&quot; - which includes treason against the government - can be punished by death, including by crucifixion if the judge so wishes; and there are religious leaders pushing for the minimum marriage age for girls to be eight years old (15 is the &quot;official&quot; age of consent, but court rulings frequently allow girls as young as 10 to be married). This is on top of all the usual police brutality and disinterest in human rights that come with any dictatorship.<br /> <br /> And yes, in the World of Darkness, this is rather grimmer, as the people in power are a little bit more heartless and fanatical, the people on the bottom are a little bit angrier, and the shadows are full of unfriendly spirits, inhuman predators and unfathomable conspiracies.<br /> <br /> As a side note, Given the Ahl i Batin's focus on unity, you probably have a fair number following the Baha'i faith, as well as a small Christian minority (Lebanese Maronites, Egyptian Copts, Assyrians, Armenians).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T13:33:45-07:00","id":1083653,"title":"","content":"Batini don't control the world. They were very powerful in an age where the Islam was a more tolerant enlightened religion than Christianity, now they don't have the amount of power than they had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T14:12:42-07:00","id":1083683,"title":"","content":"Thoughts: Lost Paths is terrible and you should ignore it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T18:58:32-07:00","id":1083778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083601-batini-and-iran?p=1083683#post1083683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts: Lost Paths is terrible and you should ignore it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah...this is the book where it was stated as fact that the prophet Muhammad was a patsy by the Ahl-I-Batin, who tormented him with voices in his head until he agreed to spread their ideas.<br /> <br /> Even the Revised Order of Hermes book didn't drop the ball on unfortunate and insensitive implications when it implied Jesus was &quot;just&quot; a mage. At least there, it was a passing mention in a footnote in the Order's timeline. And it would make perfect sense for the Hermetics to think that, since they're the kind of mystics who insist on pigeon-holing everything, in the interests of neat, tidy categorization. <i>Lost Paths</i>, meanwhile, implied that an entire religion was <i>outright invalid</i>, based on a lie started by a shadowy cabal of mystic manipulators. If I were a Muslim, I'd be offended as hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T22:42:04-07:00","id":1083861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083601-batini-and-iran?p=1083778#post1083778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah...this is the book where it was stated as fact that the prophet Muhammad was a patsy by the Ahl-I-Batin, who tormented him with voices in his head until he agreed to spread their ideas.<br /> <br /> Even the Revised Order of Hermes book didn't drop the ball on unfortunate and insensitive implications when it implied Jesus was &quot;just&quot; a mage. At least there, it was a passing mention in a footnote in the Order's timeline. And it would make perfect sense for the Hermetics to think that, since they're the kind of mystics who insist on pigeon-holing everything, in the interests of neat, tidy categorization. <i>Lost Paths</i>, meanwhile, implied that an entire religion was <i>outright invalid</i>, based on a lie started by a shadowy cabal of mystic manipulators. If I were a Muslim, I'd be offended as hell.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> well lost paths does say(IIRC) that muhammad also said several things of his own which puzzled his batini &quot;masters&quot; also keep in mind that the batini genuinely believed it to be the truth. after all most are muslims to this day not crypto zoroastrians(or whatever)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T23:58:04-07:00","id":1083877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083601-batini-and-iran?p=1083861#post1083861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> well lost paths does say(IIRC) that muhammad also said several things of his own which puzzled his batini &quot;masters&quot; also keep in mind that the batini genuinely believed it to be the truth. after all most are muslims to this day not crypto zoroastrians(or whatever)</div> </div> </div> </div>That still doesn't actually make it okay. &quot;Added several things of his own&quot; implies the bulk of the Koran is of Batini invention. And that's not okay. Probably.<br /> <br /> It becomes difficult to justify the Batini believing in the authenticity of Islam - the religion most of them subscribe to - if they also know for a fact that the old Batini masters foisted their ideas of Unity on some random guy, regardless of whether what he may or may not have &quot;added&quot; on his own.<br /> <br /> Moreover, let's take a step back and examine this from a metatextual standpoint. Why did this particular bit of historical revisionism need to be made? What purpose does it serve to make Muhammad secretly a patsy for the Ahl-I-Batin? How does knowing that detail make the Ahl-I-Batin <i>better</i>?<br /> <br /> Because it looks very much to me that the writers behind Lost Paths wanted the Batini to come off as Super Special Awesome, so they made them the de facto real founders of Islam. That they were apparently preaching its message centuries before it was even established. And that makes this Craft seem cooler...somehow. It's the same logic behind why the Batini were founded by fusing members of two different existing Traditions together (both philosophically and literally). Why the Batini were stated as having inherited souls/avatars from a previous universe altogether. And why they were given not just a prohibition from learning Entropy, but a <i>categorical inability</i> to do so. Because reasons, and because the writers wanted them to seem mysterious and cool.<br /> <br /> If I haven't made it clear before, I'm biased against the Ahl-I-Batin. Always rubbed me the wrong way, and how White Wolf treated them like the favored children. But <i>Lost Paths</i>, for me, pushed them into the realm of the reprehensible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T06:56:33-07:00","id":1083945,"title":"","content":"That's my general problem with the Batini too. I like them as a faction, but they are too often described as more special or 'in the know' than anyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T10:28:39-07:00","id":1084050,"title":"","content":"I admit, not being Muslim, I've never felt comfortable weighing in on that Lost Paths assertion about Islam. I've always decided that were I to use Lost Paths in one of my games, that the Muhammed bit would be an in character assertion. It would seem appropriate that certain Batini <i>believe</i> their ancestors/predecessors influenced the foundation of Islam, but that may just be usual Mage hubris at work.<br /> <br /> In terms of the Iran situation...I've also always gone with the idea that while individual Mages might end up being in powerful positions, the Crafts or Traditions as a whole avoid worldly politics. And there's nothing to say that an individual mage can't be corrupt, evil, or act against their group's philosophies for their own individual reasons. So even if you do decide to use WoD canon that a real person is a Mage, that doesn't mean the entire Tradition/Craft is involved or condones the real world situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T11:59:32-07:00","id":1084089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit, not being Muslim, I've never felt comfortable weighing in on that Lost Paths assertion about Islam. I've always decided that were I to use Lost Paths in one of my games, that the Muhammed bit would be an in character assertion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, totally. I think that Batini are a GREAT Craft, with the exeption of that part. From all the crafts, I find it to be one of the most flavorfull. Of curse, that's only if you grab the bit of &quot;lore&quot; that was mentioned above and put it where the sun doesn't shine. I also don't like that their lack of Entropy (because the reason given it's bullshit).<br /> <br /> Ahl i Batin have a very intereresting background (if we ignore that part among others). For instance, did you know that Al-Batin or Allah Batin it's one of the names of Allah? It's the Hidden One, a name asociated with the occult and the esoteric aspects of the religion. The focus on labyrinths and secrets that the Craft has go well with that. I also like the Sufi shtick that they have, that it's favored by this focus on subtlety (with things like &quot;the science of absense&quot; and &quot;the hidden sufi&quot; being part of Sufi tradition, if my sources ain't wrong). I think that a bit of this would be lost if they were to be put in the always hopeful Celestial Chorus, so I'm glad they exist (though I'm not so glad Lost Paths exists).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T12:27:24-07:00","id":1084098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083601-batini-and-iran?p=1083945#post1083945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's my general problem with the Batini too. I like them as a faction, but they are too often described as more special or 'in the know' than anyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> technically speaking from a metagame perspective they are<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> anyway as for batini being muslims keep in mind that even the most devout of them are supposed to be very tolerant of diverse views AKA they're heretical from a real life point of view.<br /> <br /> finally,perhaps it's because im personally agnostic-leaning atheist.. but i don't mind if a book in a <b>game</b> says something that might be insultive of a religion(so long as this is not the reason d'etre itsself) after all,the world of darkness is not our world it's islam is not our islam and the batini are definetely not real...or are they??!!!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T18:27:53-07:00","id":1084226,"title":"","content":"Some of that problem, as far as Lost Paths went, is that Kraig Blackwelder always seemed to have a compulsion to present whatever group he was writing about as some how more cooler, capable and just in every way better than anyone else. You see the same thing in the Bone Flowers book for KotE and with the Teragen in his entire run as Aberrant developer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T21:47:49-07:00","id":1084332,"title":"","content":"I'm now thinking politically incorrect thoughts about a group called the Talibatini, a terrorist group with Arcane so high no one remembers their acts of terrorism or attributes these to someone else. Also, sometimes they phase in and out of existence during critical moments. I want to involve Achmed the dead terrorist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.th